    "_notes": "Bosch BME690 (temperature, pressure, humidity, gas) at 0x76 (SDO low) or 0x77 (SDO high). Detection: chip ID (0xD0) 0x61 and variant (0xF0) 0x02 - the BME680 (variant 0x00) and BME688 (0x01) share the chip ID but not the formulas or layout. Forced mode only: each poll triggers a measurement (ctrl_meas 0x74 = 0x25: temperature and pressure x1, forced), waits 200 ms (TPH plus the 152 ms heater time) and reads the calibration (0x8A 23, 0xE1 14, 0x00 5 bytes - Bosch's 42-byte coefficient array) and the data (0x1D 17 bytes: 24-bit pressure and temperature, 16-bit humidity, 10-bit gas at bytes 15-16); the decode code applies the floating-point formulas of Bosch's BME690 SensorAPI (bme69x.c v1.1.0), with gas 0 unless gas valid and heater stable are both set. Init: soft reset, 10 ms; ctrl_hum 0x01; config 0x00; gas_wait_0 0x66 (152 ms); res_heat_0 0x69; ctrl_gas_1 0x20 (run gas, profile 0). res_heat_0 is FIXED, as for the BME680: 0x69 is one unit's value for 320 C (0x68-0x69 over 15-35 C ambient), so the hot plate temperature differs between units and gas resistance is a relative trend - see devdocs/computed-init-values.md. 0x76 is also a common multiplexer address.",
